================================================================================
1. Original work by The Abstract Lab
================================================================================

Developed by The Abstract Lab and licensed under Apache-2.0:

  - The Python runtime architecture: model lifecycle, StatePool, process and
    phase scheduler, MPI communication, checkpoint semantics, history output,
    plugin API, and the Python-owned control path over the original CAM.
  - The decomposable device/kernel model: device descriptors, the device and
    kernel code generators, the generic pointer/rank/shape ABI, the state
    bridge generator, and the generated bind(C) adapters.
  - The build, validation, and tooling layers under tools/, jobs/, tests/,
    and validation/ (excluding the patch files listed in section 3).
  - The configuration files under configs/ and devices/overrides.yaml.

  - The reference case script under reference/, which drives an unmodified
    upstream case and contains no upstream source.

Except where section 2, 3, or 4 says otherwise, everything in src/freecam/,
native/, tools/, tests/, jobs/, configs/, docs/, examples/, reference/, and
validation/ is original work.


