2. Algorithms transcribed from CESM / CAM / HOMME
================================================================================

Copyright (c) 2017, University Corporation for Atmospheric Research (UCAR)
Licensed under a BSD 3-Clause license: LICENSES/UCAR-CESM-BSD-3-Clause.txt

freeCAM reproduces the numerical behavior of specific CESM/CAM routines
bit-for-bit. To do that, the routines below were transcribed from the pinned
CESM sources into Fortran compilation units or into Python. They preserve the
upstream expression order and are derivative works of the UCAR sources; they
are not new numerical formulations. Each transcription names its upstream
routine in a comment or docstring at the point of definition.

Fortran transcriptions:

  native/kernels/se_limiter_reference.F90
      from CAM SE dycore: limiter_optim_iter_full
  native/kernels/hydrostatic_energy_reference.F90
      from CAM cam_thermo: get_hydrostatic_energy_1hd
  native/kernels/hypervis_reference_support.F90
      from CAM SE dycore: get_dp_ref

Python transcriptions (23 routines; see the "Port ..." docstrings):

  src/freecam/model/se_runtime.py
      subcell_Laplace_fluxes, dyn_comp:stepon forcing normalization,
      prim_advance_mod:ApplyCAMForcing, prim_advance_mod:compute_and_apply_rhs,
      SE/FVM v1 biharmonic diffusion and sponge, euler_step limiter-8,
      and CAM's active-water thermodynamic helper calls
  src/freecam/model/phases.py
      dyn2fvm_mass_vars, SE derived_phys_dry (FKESSLER subset),
      gws_src_vort, gws_src_fnct,
      gravity_waves_sources::compute_vertical_derivative,
      cam_thermo:get_hydrostatic_energy_1hd (active loop)
  src/freecam/model/grid.py
      spacecurve_mod::GenSpaceCurve, cart2cubedsphere, cubedsphere2cart
  src/freecam/model/fvm_mapping.py
      fvm_mapping:lagrange_1d, fvm_mapping:tensor_lagrange_interp limiter,
      SE/FVM p_d_coupling forcing boundary
  src/freecam/model/scientific_data.py
      interpolate_data::lininterp_init, lininterp2d1d
  src/freecam/model/initialization.py
      CAM-SE prim_set_dry_mass
  src/freecam/model/dynamics.py
      compute_omega including DSS and the startup biharmonic filter

Interface-level derivation: the bind(C) wrappers in
native/kernels/fvm_transport_kernel.F90, native/kernels/fvm_displacement_kernel.F90,
native/kernels/remap_support.F90, and native/kernels/se_startup_kernel.F90 call
upstream modules (fvm_consistent_se_cslam, dimensions_mod, fv_mapz, and others)
and therefore reproduce their argument contracts. The upstream numerical bodies
themselves are NOT contained in this repository; they are compiled at build time
from the pinned upstream checkout.


