================================================================================
4. Generated descriptors derived from upstream metadata
================================================================================

The files under devices/generated/ are generated by freeCAM's own tooling from
the CCPP metadata (.meta) of the pinned CAM-SIMA checkout. They record argument
names, standard names, dtypes, ranks, intents, and lifecycle entry points that
originate in upstream metadata authored by UCAR/NCAR and the CCPP community
(LICENSES/CCPP-Atmospheric-Physics-Apache-2.0.txt,
LICENSES/CCPP-Framework-Apache-2.0.txt). They contain no upstream source code.


================================================================================
5. Interface providers that are NOT upstream copies
================================================================================

The modules under native/devices/support/ and the stub modules in
native/kernels/fvm_kernel_stubs.F90 and native/kernels/remap_stubs.F90 reuse
upstream module names, symbol names, and public parameter names (shr_kind_mod,
ccpp_kinds, physconst, ppgrid, ref_pres, cam_logfile, cam_abortutils,
shr_sys_mod, shr_log_mod, shr_assert_mod, spmd_utils, control_mod, perf_mod,
cam_time_coord, error_messages, musica_ccpp_namelist, and others) so that
unmodified upstream schemes link against them.

These are new implementations written for this project. They are not copies of,
and were not derived from, the upstream module bodies. They exist only to
satisfy the link-time interface while keeping the corresponding services
Python-owned.


================================================================================
6. Upstream code that is pinned but NOT redistributed
================================================================================

freeCAM references upstream trees as git submodules and builds against them; it
does not vendor their sources and does not ship their build products:

  external/CAM-SIMA           ESCOMP/CAM-SIMA @ f8daa568eae2696b7c4ebff7768f02f5d097d9df
  external/iCESM1.3.1_fzhu    NCAR/iCESM1.3_iHESP_hires @ 556ad1c112af6606299f8270ad6f8b9b16540332
                              (tag iCESM1.3.1; CAM pinned to iCAM5_iHESP
                              commit 09c8a19c463122fad488e6fd1bbc0fcd0f410130)

This distinction matters. The CESM copyright notice
(LICENSES/CESM-Copyright-Notice.txt) places most of CESM in the public domain
but carves out segregable components that keep their own, in some cases more
restrictive, terms -- among them ESMF (University of Illinois/NCSA), POP, SCRIP
and CICE (Los Alamos National Security), CISM (LGPL v3), AER RRTMG, MCT
(UChicago Argonne), the ISCCP simulator, XML/Lite, and Lahey's
Inf_NaN_Detection module, whose terms forbid selling copies or standalone
compiled files derived from it without permission from Lahey Computer Systems.

Building a CAM shared library from the pinned tree links several of these
components. Redistributing such a binary would redistribute them, and the terms
above -- not this NOTICE -- would govern. freeCAM therefore builds from pinned
upstream sources on the target machine and does not distribute compiled model
libraries. See the "Licensing and redistribution" section of README.md.
